{"id":"baanah","name":"Baanah","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:baanah"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Baanah","text":"Son of affliction. (1.) One of the two sons of Rimmon the Beerothite, a captain in Saul’s army. He and his brother Rechab assassinated Ishbosheth (2 Sam. 4:2), and were on this account slain by David, and their mutilated bodies suspended over the pool at Hebron (5, 6, 12). (2.) The father of Heled, who was one of David’s thirty heroes (2 Sam. 23:29; 1 Chr. 11:30)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H1196","lemma":"בַּעֲנָה","xlit":"Baʻănâh","gloss":"Baanah, the name of four Israelites","kjv":"Baanah","count":9,"share":0.9},{"strong":"H7394","lemma":"רֵכָב","xlit":"Rêkâb","gloss":"Rekab, the name of two Arabs and of two Israelites","kjv":"Rechab","count":4,"share":0.4},{"strong":"H886","lemma":"בְּאֵרֹתִי","xlit":"Bᵉʼêrôthîy","gloss":"a Beerothite or inhabitant of Beeroth","kjv":"Beerothite","count":3,"share":0.3},{"strong":"H7417","lemma":"רִמּוֹן","xlit":"Rimmôwn","gloss":"Rimmon, the name of a Syrian deity, also of five places","kjv":"Remmon, Rimmon","count":3,"share":0.3},{"strong":"H1114","lemma":"בִּלְשָׁן","xlit":"Bilshân","gloss":"Bilshan, an Israelite","kjv":"Bilshan","count":2,"share":0.2},{"strong":"H902","lemma":"בִּגְוַי","xlit":"Bigvay","gloss":"Bigvai, an Israelite","kjv":"Bigvai","count":2,"share":0.2}],"verses":["2Sam.4.2","2Sam.4.5","2Sam.4.6","2Sam.4.9","2Sam.23.29","1Chr.11.30","Ezra.2.2","Neh.7.7","Neh.10.27","1Kgs.4.16"],"related":[{"id":"rimmon","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.143,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"rechab","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.125,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"ish-bosheth","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.1,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"assassination","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.097,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"rechab","type":"lexical","strong":"H7394","why":"both l